========================================
 SUMMARY
========================================
- TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1 are enabled (deprecated, RFC 8996); TLSv1.3 is
  not supported
- TLS_FALLBACK_SCSV (RFC 7507) is not supported -> vulnerable to
  downgrade attacks
- Heartbleed: not vulnerable across all tested protocol versions
- Certificate: RSA 2048-bit, sha256WithRSAEncryption, issued by
  Sectigo, valid May 2025 - Jun 2026, CN/SAN = demo.testfire.net
- DHE cipher suites observed using only 1024-bit DH groups
  (see testssl_result.txt for confirmed Logjam finding)
- Full ciphers accepted across TLSv1.0/1.1/1.2 exceed current best
  practice (legacy CBC and SHA1-based suites still offered)
